{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>See, I have given into your hand Sihon</b> — teaches that He showed him the prince of Sihon bound in his hand." "<b>Begin</b> — four times in the Masorah: החל here, and the other החל וכלה, and וגלות החל, and החל רש. החל וכלה — for they were causing the nations to inherit, about whom it is said: לא תחיה כל נשמה. וגלות החל — teaches that He hinted to Moses the exile. Alternatively: just as here it is written החל רש, so too there it is written: ירשו את ערי הנגב. And as stated in Tanḥuma: all the miracles that HaShem performed in the wilderness are destined to be performed for Israel in Zion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The phrase 'שהיו משכעה עממין' is obscure; translated hyper-literally as 'for they were causing the nations to inherit.' The four-fold masorah count lists החל occurrences across Scripture."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:38.403017489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}